messages:
Lena: Quick run — dark console: token chip hover looks like a spotlight, and chart mid-series wash out. Can we iterate?
Omar: Yup. My vote: flatten hover (lower saturation) + subtle inset. Try hover #181a1c.
Priya: For charts, warm mid palette + optional hatch patterns. Add toggle under Settings > Accessibility.
Sam: CSS snippet to try:
```css
:root[data-theme='dark']{
  --chip-bg:#0b0c0d;
  --chip-hover:#181a1c;
  --chip-focus:rgba(255,255,255,0.06);
}
.chip{background:var(--chip-bg);}
.chip:hover{background:var(--chip-hover);box-shadow:inset 0 -1px 0 rgba(0,0,0,0.35);}
.chip:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--chip-focus);}
```
Lena: Nice. Micro-copy for toggle? "Accessible chart patterns" + tooltip "Overlay patterns when colors are hard to tell apart."
Omar: Also add dev flag `--force-chart-patterns` and analytics event when auto-enabled.
design-bot: Tokens proposed (staging): --chip-hover:#181a1c, --code-inline-bg:rgba(6,7,8,0.45), --chart-patterns-enabled:false.
